# use — success
#
# USE carried through at a station nobody owns: the ruin's old anvil, worked as a blacksmith with the
# trade's own hammer (accepted without a critic call). Success opens the crafting menu; an iron bar is
# broken down for its eight units of metal and two horseshoes are made from them, and what is left is
# thrown away on leaving.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --grant-mm blacksmithing --grant-item hammer,iron_bar --location-type test --location-id 0 --start-area "Test Ruin" --period dawn --observe-only "Test Old Anvil"

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

strategy succeed
goal use
means blacksmithing
advance 12 180

click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180

# The hammer is the blacksmith's own implement: MadeForIt, no critic.
click action 0
choose 1
regions
choose 0
advance 12 180

regions
click action 1
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180

expect SUCCESS
expect At work:
expect-verb use
expect-outcome crafting_opened

# The menu is held for the CONTINUE, so the chips above could be read before it takes the screen.
click button
wait mode Crafting 30

expect-state crafting trade=blacksmithing material=metal pool=0
expect-state crafting crafting break item=iron_bar units=8
craft break Iron Bar
expect-state crafting pool=8
craft make horseshoe
craft make horseshoe
expect-state crafting pool=4
craft leave
wait mode LocationInteraction 30

expect-state items horseshoe
expect-no-state items iron_bar
quit
